    "fp": "A page that documents a private range as an example may still be reported; confirm it is static text.",
    "recordDesc": "A private-range IPv4 address in a response gives every reader the same view the bank has internally: The address maps the internal network the application talks to, and combined with an SSRF primitive it becomes a set of targets rather than a guess.",
    "applicability": "Debug pages, proxy error messages and client configuration that lists upstream hosts.",
    "risk": "An internal address is the first hop of lateral movement and is worthless to a browser.",
    "why": "Internal topology is server-side information that never needed to be in the response.",
    "fix": [
      "Strip internal addresses from every rendered error and configuration page.",
      "Block outbound requests to private ranges from the application tier."
