    "title": "Software licence key in a response",
    "description": "A licence key or serial number field appears in the response body. A licence key is a credential for a paid product; published in a page it invites reuse and, for server products, can unlock the same edition elsewhere.",
    "remediation": "Remove the key from the response, keep it in the licence server and show only the edition and expiry.",
    "limitation": "One response body. It matches a licence field followed by a grouped key, not the product name.",
    "scopeT": "One response body. It matches a licence field followed by a grouped key, not the product name.",
    "fp": "A page that lists licence terms without a key is not reported.",
    "recordDesc": "A licence key or serial number field in a response gives every reader the same view the bank has internally: A licence key is a credential for a paid product; published in a page it invites reuse and, for server products, can unlock the same edition elsewhere.",
    "applicability": "Admin consoles, about pages and support bundles.",
    "risk": "Key reuse undermines the vendor contract and can expose the account the key is bound to.",
    "why": "A licence key is transferable by design, so it must be treated as a secret.",
    "fix": [
      "Remove the key from every rendered page and support bundle.",
      "Show the edition and expiry date instead."
    ],
    "verifyT": "Open the about page and confirm no licence key is returned.",
